    "narrative": "LawDog faces a favorable slate today, particularly against Ritchie, whose 4.93 xERA anchors several of our strongest plays. The top of our lineup is headlined by **Geraldo Perdomo** (72.67), who capitalizes on a high-ceiling matchup against Aldegheri, and **Tyler Freeman** (71.10). While **Tyler Freeman** holds a stellar projection due to his #2 spot in the order and a favorable park, managers should monitor the 43% rain risk in his contest; a delay or cancellation could necessitate a pivot. Meanwhile, **Matt Chapman** (70.21) remains a high-floor anchor at the hot corner, buoyed by the weak SP matchup and a top-three lineup placement that maximizes his RBI opportunities. \n\nOur core of contact hitters\u2014**Luis Arraez** (66.78) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65)\u2014are prime starters today, as their high-contact profiles align perfectly against the exploitable Ritchie. **Bryson Stott** (66.64) also earns a strong start, with a significant 13% dynamic platoon boost helping him overcome a minor BvP historical drag. On the bubble, **Taylor Ward** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine; his 45.20 score narrowly missed the cut due to the \"Lineup Pending\" status and a difficult matchup against Kirby, which suppressed his potential ceiling compared to the primary lineup's favorable matchups. We will keep **Taylor Ward** on high alert should any late scratch occur, though he remains a bench pivot today while we prioritize the superior matchup data driving the current starting roster.",
